// Visual Studio in its dark theme, as near as the flat skin gets to it. Near black greys with no blue in them, hairline
// borders a shade lighter, nothing round and the rows packed tight, the way the 2022 one is drawn. The code in its colours
// for C#, blue keywords, pink ones that send the code somewhere, teal types, pale yellow methods, light blue locals and
// parameters, brown texts and green comments, which every other language gets too. The caret is the text's own grey and
// the terminals are in Windows Terminal's Campbell, which is what Visual Studio's own terminal is in. The Visual Studio
// look of Hex's puts this on with the glass and the lights off and the code in Cascadia Mono.

